\newlabel{fig:per_multiplier_radar}{{B.1}{5}{\textbf {Per-multiplier behavioural metrics.} We report four standardised metrics defined in the FAIRGAME framework~\cite {buscemi2025fairgame}: (1) \textbf {Internal Variability (IV)}, which quantifies the stochasticity of an agent's behaviour by measuring the variance of outcomes across identical experimental repetitions; (2) \textbf {Cross-Language Inconsistency (CI)}, which measures the standard deviation of agent performance across the five tested languages to indicate sensitivity to linguistic framing; (3) \textbf {Variability over Round (VR)}, which captures the volatility of decision-making and strategy changes throughout the 10-round game horizon; and (4) \textbf {Sensitivity-to-Payoff (SP)}, which reflects the magnitude of behavioural adaptation in response to varying incentive stakes. Radar charts compare Mistral Large (green), Claude 3.5 Haiku (orange), and GPT-4o (blue) across three payoff scales ($\lambda \in \{0.1, 1, 10\}$). Compared to the baseline payoff ($\lambda =1$), similar scores are observed for the higher stake payoff ($\lambda =10$). At low stakes ($\lambda =0.1$), models exhibit divergent scores. Overall, internal variability (IV) is most affected by varying the payoff stake}{figure.B.1}{}}
